Title: Fifa Club World Cup criticised by player union Fifpro
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Sergio Marchi', 'Text': 'What was presented as a global celebration of football was nothing more than a fiction created by Fifa, promoted by its president, without dialogue, sensitivity, and respect for those who sustain the game with their daily efforts.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 8, 'EndChar': 177}}, {'Speaker': 'Sergio Marchi', 'Text': "A grandiloquent staging inevitably reminiscent of the 'bread and circuses' of Nero's Rome, entertainment for the masses while behind the scenes inequality, precariousness, and the lack of protection for the true protagonists deepen.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 203}}, {'Speaker': 'Sergio Marchi', 'Text': "the tournament was held under unacceptable conditions… that put the players' physical integrity at risk", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 13, 'StartChar': 14, 'EndChar': 90}}, {'Speaker': 'Sergio Marchi', 'Text': "This situation must not only be denounced, but must be firmly warned against. What happened cannot be repeated under any circumstances at next year's Fifa World Cup.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 10, 'EndChar': 163}}, {'Speaker': 'Sergio Marchi', 'Text': "We have been warning about the overcrowded schedule, the lack of physical and mental rest for players, and the lack of dialogue on the part of Fifa. This way of organising tournaments, without listening to the federation that represents the world's professional footballers' associations, is unilateral, authoritarian, and based solely on a logic of economic profitability, not human sustainability.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 316}}, {'Speaker': 'Sergio Marchi', 'Text': 'We cannot continue to play with the health of players to fuel a marketing machine. There is no spectacle possible if the voices of the protagonists are silenced.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 16, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 148}}], 'Description': [{'Description': "In a scathing statement, Sergio Marchi appeared to compare the world governing body's president Gianni Infantino to the Roman emperor Nero.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 109}}, {'Description': 'And he also claimed Fifa "chose to continue increasing its revenue at the expense of the players\' bodies and health".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 101}}, {'Description': 'It comes after BBC Sport learned that Fifpro was not invited to a key meeting on player welfare that Infantino held on the eve of the Club World Cup final with representatives from other unions.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 181}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Fifa president Gianni Infantino'}]}
